##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# GitHub issue #3 (spec 017, US1) regression: occlusion() silently no-ops
# under the JIT. numthreads 1 required: occlusion() is a raytraced,
# RNG-adjacent lookup (12-sample hemisphere AO), same thread-scheduling-
# sensitivity confirmed for random() during issue #1's fix.
#
# A lone convex sphere has exactly zero ambient occlusion everywhere (no
# other geometry to block any hemisphere sample) -- a degenerate,
# non-discriminating test. A second, smaller (overlapping) sphere creates
# genuine partial occlusion, giving a visibly varying 0..1 pattern.
# Investigation note: the occluder needs an explicit
# Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1] -- ray-visibility categories
# (diffuse/specular/transmission) default OFF (CAttributes::CAttributes(),
# attributes.cpp:87-93, only sets PRIMARY_VISIBLE/DOUBLE_SIDED/
# DISPLACEMENTS by default) -- without it every AO hemisphere ray misses
# the occluder and occlusion() returns exactly 0 everywhere, which read
# as a bug during initial investigation but is correct, documented
# scene-setup behavior once traced through CAttributes' default flags.
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
Option "limits" "numthreads" [1]
Display "sphere-occlusion-reyes.tif" "file" "rgba"
Projection "perspective"
Clipping 0.1 100
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
  Surface "occlusion_probe"
  Sphere 1 -1 1 360
  AttributeBegin
    Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1]
    Surface "matte"
    Translate 1.2 0 -0.5
    Sphere 0.9 -0.9 0.9 360
  AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
